Subject: Reduce-Entity-Tick-Allocations

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Vanilla entity ticking allocates many short-lived objects per-tick:
AABB instances, BlockPos sets, random numbers, collision shapes.
These allocations pressure the garbage collector and cause latency
spikes during collections. Moonrise provides optimized implementations
that reuse objects where possible.

Impact:
Lower GC pressure, fewer and shorter GC pauses, more consistent
tick times under heavy entity load.

Migration Note:
This patch enables Moonrise's entity tick allocation optimizations.
The key changes are in entity collision handling, fluid state
lookups, and random number generation.
